# These go to eleven (0.17.83): a knob that runs 0-100 and shows a plain 100 has one more notch, reading 11 in red. The setting stays 100;
# a notch down is 100 again. A knob with a unit or a name (or another range) stops at its top as before.
seed 0
wait 3000
tap ENV
wait 200
expect view 1
spin K1 120
wait 100
expect par0 100
spin K1 1
wait 100
expect par0 100
expect eleven 0
shot eleven.png
spin K1 3
wait 100
expect eleven 0
expect par0 100
spin K1 -1
wait 100
expect eleven -1
expect par0 100
spin K1 -1
wait 100
expect par0 99
# Bright (also 0-100, a plain number): the same
spin K2 120
spin K2 1
wait 100
expect eleven 9
expect par9 100
# turning another knob up to its top moves the eleven there; a value moved some other way lets go of it
spin K2 -5
wait 100
expect eleven -1
expect par9 96
